---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Engineering | Bauhu" description="Engineering and resilience information for Bauhu building systems.">
  <SiteHeader />
  <main class="bg-paper">
    <section class="relative flex min-h-[82vh] items-end overflow-hidden bg-ink text-paper">
      <img src="/images/developments/bauhu-engineering-hero.webp" alt="Bauhu engineering and construction system" class="absolute inset-0 h-full w-full object-cover" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" />
      <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-t from-ink/90 via-ink/45 to-ink/20"></div>
      <div class="relative z-10 mx-auto grid w-full max-w-site gap-12 px-5 pb-16 pt-36 lg:grid-cols-[0.9fr_1.1fr] lg:px-10 lg:pb-20">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow text-stone">Engineering</p>
          <h1 class="mt-5 max-w-4xl font-display text-5xl leading-tight md:text-7xl">Designed for demanding coastal sites.</h1>
        </div>
        <div class="self-end space-y-7 text-lg leading-8 text-paper/75">
          <p>Bauhu homes are designed around more than appearance. The building system, structure, shipping method, site handling and local completion route all need to work together.</p>
          <p>This matters most in remote, coastal and hurricane exposed locations, where conventional construction can become slow, uncertain and difficult to control.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-pad bg-mist">
      <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-site gap-5 md:grid-cols-3">
        <article class="bg-paper p-7">
          <p class="eyebrow text-clay">System</p>
          <h2 class="mt-12 font-display text-3xl">Steel frame logic</h2>
          <p class="mt-5 leading-7 text-ink/70">A precise structural system gives each project a controlled manufactured core, reducing reliance on improvised site construction.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="bg-paper p-7">
          <p class="eyebrow text-clay">Climate</p>
          <h2 class="mt-12 font-display text-3xl">Coastal resilience</h2>
          <p class="mt-5 leading-7 text-ink/70">Homes must respond to wind, corrosion, heat, shade, maintenance and exposure from the earliest design stage.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="bg-paper p-7">
          <p class="eyebrow text-clay">Delivery</p>
          <h2 class="mt-12 font-display text-3xl">Remote logistics</h2>
          <p class="mt-5 leading-7 text-ink/70">Design and manufacture are planned around packing, shipping, unloading, site access and local completion.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-pad bg-paper">
      <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-site gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[0.9fr_1.1fr]">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow text-clay">Hurricane-exposed environments</p>
          <h2 class="mt-5 font-display text-4xl leading-tight md:text-6xl">Resilience is an engineering problem, not a marketing label.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-6 text-lg leading-8 text-ink/70">
          <p>Bauhu projects in high-wind regions are engineered around the actual site, applicable code, exposure and final building geometry. Wind loads, uplift, load paths, connections, openings and envelope strategy have to work together.</p>
          <p>We avoid treating “hurricane proof” as an absolute promise. The correct engineering response is project-specific, documented and coordinated with the rest of the building system.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="mx-auto mt-12 grid max-w-site gap-5 md:grid-cols-3">
        {['Structural frame / connection detail','Roof, uplift and load-path detail','Completed home in hurricane-exposed location'].map((label) => (
          <div class="flex min-h-64 items-center justify-center border border-ink/15 bg-mist p-6 text-center">
            <div><p class="eyebrow text-clay">IMAGE PLACEHOLDER</p><p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-6 text-ink/55">{label}</p></div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-pad bg-mist">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-site">
        <p class="eyebrow text-clay">From engineering to manufacture</p>
        <h2 class="mt-5 max-w-4xl font-display text-4xl leading-tight md:text-6xl">The detail only matters if it reaches the thing that gets built.</h2>
        <p class="mt-8 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-8 text-ink/70">Bauhu coordinates approved design information with the bill of materials, procurement and fabrication information. The purpose is straightforward: reduce the chance that the drawing, the order and the manufactured component become three different versions of the project.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-pad bg-ink text-paper">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-site">
        <p class="eyebrow text-stone">Why it matters</p>
        <h2 class="mt-5 max-w-4xl font-display text-4xl leading-tight md:text-6xl">Beautiful homes still need a serious route to being built.</h2>
        <p class="mt-8 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-8 text-paper/70">Bauhu’s value is the combination of architectural design and practical build system thinking. The aim is to create homes that are desirable to live in and realistic to deliver in locations where construction is rarely simple.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</BaseLayout>
